# Web SEO: Agent-host ecosystems

Vendor-aligned **first-class channel** relationships (Meta Muse ↔ Facebook/Instagram/Threads, Grok Bot ↔ X, OpenClaw/Dots ↔ OpenAI-personal-agents sibling grids). Single module: **`web/src/lib/content/constants/agents/ecosystems/index.ts`**.

Host picker scenarios stay in **`agents/decision-scenarios.ts`**. UI archetypes stay in **`agents/host-profiles.ts`** — do not conflate with ecosystem ids.

## Profiles (`AgentHostEcosystemId`)

| Id | Host slugs (`AGENT_HOST_ECOSYSTEM_BY_SLUG`) | First-class channels | Typical MCP pin (`relatedMcpSlugs`) |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `meta-consumer` | `meta-muse` | `facebook`, `instagram`, `threads` | `muse-code` |
| `openai-personal-agents` | `openclaw`, `dots` | — (sibling agents on host landings) | `chatgpt` |
| `xai-grok` | `grok-bot` | `x` | `grok-build`, `cursor` |
| `google-gemini` | `gemini` | `youtube` | `android-studio`, `antigravity-cli` |
| `anthropic-claude` | `claude-duet` | — (sibling MCP on host landings) | `claude-code`, `claude-cowork` |

Extend **`ECOSYSTEM_PROFILES`**, **`AGENT_HOST_ECOSYSTEM_BY_SLUG`**, and **`audienceTailoredCardByHostSlug`** together when adding a mapped host. Mapped MCP clients go in **`MCP_CLIENT_ECOSYSTEM_BY_SLUG`** + **`audienceTailoredCardByMcpSlug`** (`grok-build` → X home network, `muse-code` → Meta-owned channels first, `android-studio` / `antigravity-cli` → Gemini-first; **`cursor` → `xai-grok`** for hub grid copy). **`meta-consumer`** pins **`meta-muse`** in **`relatedAgentSlugs`** for integration grid order.

## Where copy runs

| Surface | Entry | Ecosystem behavior |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **`/agents/{host}`** | `getPublicAgentHostBySlug` → `withAgentHostEcosystem` (`agents/index.ts`) | Fourth WhoIsFor card; `buildAgentHostEcosystemFaqItems`; hub channel grid sort + badges via `sortAgentChannelHubLinks` |
| **`/agents/{mcp}`** | `getPublicMcpLandingBySlug` → `buildMcpClientEcosystemFaqItems` + `resolveMcpClientAudienceCards` | Fourth WhoIsFor card for mapped MCP clients (`grok-build`, `muse-code`); Muse Code ↔ Meta Muse FAQs; Grok Build/Cursor ↔ Grok Bot compare FAQs; hub channel grid sort + first-class badges |
| **`/agents/{host}/{channel}`** | `buildAgentChannelLandingVm` | **`buildAgentsChannelAudienceSection`** → **`resolveAgentChannelAudienceCards`**; not `/channels/{slug}` inverse card. See **WhoIsFor assembly** below |
| **`/agents/{mcp}/{channel}`** | `buildMcpChannelLandingVm` | Same pattern with **`resolveMcpChannelAudienceCards`**. Do **not** append `buildPublicChannelEcosystemAudienceTailoredCard` — `/channels/{slug}` only |
| **`/channels/{slug}`** | `getPublicChannelBySlug` → `withChannelPageSeoCopy` (`channels/index.ts`) | **Inverse** emphasis: ecosystem fourth card (`buildPublicChannelEcosystemAudienceTailoredCard`), first-card hook (`applyPublicChannelPageAudienceFirstCardHook`), prepended FAQs (`buildPublicChannelEcosystemFaqItems`, dedupe by title), then `PUBLIC_CHANNELS_HUB_FAQ_ITEM_IDS` |
| **`/channels/{slug}` grids** | `channelPageSeo.ts`, grid copy utils, `listPublicAgentIntegrationsForChannel` | Pinned agent hosts (`CHANNEL_PAGE_PINNED_AGENT_SLUGS`); MCP sort via `sortAgentIntegrationsForEcosystem` + primary host from `getPrimaryAgentHostSlugForChannelPage`; sibling badges (`enrichPublicChannelSiblingGridItems`) |

**`/channels/{slug}`:** three base `audienceCards` + optional seed **`audienceTailoredCard`** (e.g. Reddit moderators) + runtime fourth — see `resolvePublicChannelAudienceCards`. Do **not** paste ecosystem fourth cards into catalog seeds.

**`/agents/{host|mcp}/{channel}` — WhoIsFor assembly (max `MAX_AGENT_CHANNEL_AUDIENCE_CARDS` = 6):**

1. **Three** social seed personas — `buildAgentsChannelAudienceSection` slices longer channel seeds (Developers / Agent operators stay on `/channels/{slug}` only).
2. Optional seed **`audienceTailoredCard`** — must not repeat a seed **title** (merge overlapping B2B angles into an existing card instead).
3. Ecosystem card — `appendEcosystemAudienceCardForAgentChannel`; on **non–first-class** channels, description pairs **this channel + vendor first-class networks** (e.g. TikTok + Meta). First-class pages keep static host/MCP card + API line on card 0 hook only.
4. Official-API / ban safety — **`agents/officialApiAudience.ts`** via `resolveAgentChannelAudienceCards`. Skipped when **first-class** for host, when **`shouldSkipOfficialApiAgentChannelCard`** (TikTok — ban copy on seed card 1), or directory. **Reddit:** human handoff, not OAuth publish.

**`/agents/{host}`:** `resolveAgentHostAudienceCards` appends shared **Creators who fear platform bans** — do **not** duplicate in host seed `audienceCards`.

**Hub grid** (`PublicChannelSiblingGrid`): `buildAgentHostEcosystemChannelSiblingGridHubTitle` / `Description` use **`getLandingEcosystemId`** (host + MCP slugs).

Generic fallback when no ecosystem: **`buildPublicChannelAgentAudienceTailoredCard`** in `channelPageSeo.ts`.

## Key symbols (channel page)

- `getChannelPageEcosystemId`, `getPrimaryAgentHostSlugForChannelPage`
- `buildPublicChannelEcosystemAudienceTailoredCard`, `buildPublicChannelEcosystemFaqItems`
- `buildPublicChannelAgentIntegrationsGridTitle(platformLabel, channelSlug)` — pass **`channelSlug`** from templates for ecosystem titles
- `buildPublicChannelSiblingGridDescription(platformLabel, channelSlug)`

## FAQ deduplication

- Host seed FAQs + `buildAgentHostEcosystemFaqItems` must not repeat the same **`title`** (tests in `ecosystems.test.ts`). MCP seeds + `buildMcpClientEcosystemFaqItems` follow the same rule (`getPublicMcpLandingBySlug`).
- Channel pages: prepend ecosystem FAQs only when titles are absent from seed **`faqItems`**.
- OpenAI-personal-agents host ecosystem FAQ builder intentionally returns `[]` — use host **`buildAgentHostPickerFaqDescription`** on OpenClaw/Dots seeds instead.

## Tests

| File | Covers |
| --- | --- |
| `ecosystems/ecosystems.test.ts` | Maps, sort, host FAQ, channel id lookup, MCP pins |
| `channels/catalog/channelPageSeo.test.ts` | `/channels/x` WhoIsFor + Grok pin order |
| `buildPublicChannelAgentIntegrationsGridCopy.test.ts` | Ecosystem integration titles + list order |

Mock hub links in tests: use **`PublicAgentChannelHubLinkViewModel`** and **`icons.*.name`** (`TikTok`, not `Tiktok`).

## Do not (WhoIsFor)

- Duplicate official-API / ban safety in host seeds or a second channel card when `officialApiAudience.ts` or seed tailoring already covers it.
- Add **`audienceTailoredCard`** that overlaps a seed persona title or ecosystem card theme.
- Ship **more than six** WhoIsFor cards on agent × channel landings.

## PR checklist (ecosystem touch)

- [ ] Host slug registered in **`AGENT_HOST_ECOSYSTEM_BY_SLUG`** only when product claims a first-class or sibling relationship; MCP slugs in **`MCP_CLIENT_ECOSYSTEM_BY_SLUG`** when hub grid / fourth card applies
- [ ] **`/channels/{slug}`**, **`/agents/{host}`**, one **`/agents/{host}/{channel}`** smoke: WhoIsFor count ≤ 6 on agent × channel, no duplicate FAQ titles, integration grid order
- [ ] **`pnpm exec vitest run`** on `ecosystems.test.ts` and channel grid copy tests
- [ ] Neutral vendor copy (**source-project-neutrality**); short sentences, no semicolon chains (**web-seo-pseo** ASD-STE100)

